834 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. Why did the crypto market experience significant drawdowns at the start of 2026? Despite a massive structural expansion in 2025, early 2026 saw Bitcoin and Ethereum face double-digit drawdowns \(reaching -14.8% and -19.6% respectively in February\) due to a combination of stalled global M2 liquidity and institutional de-risking. While specific outliers like HYPE \(+32.54%\) decoupled from the trend, the broader market was suppressed by a "wait-and-see" approach as the Federal Reserve struggled to balance cooling inflation against rising consumer financial stress.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 697 0 R
/Next 909 0 R
>>
endobj
835 0 obj
<<
/Title (5. Are institutional investors still committed to Bitcoin and Ethereum? The data shows a nuanced picture. While Asset Managers have significantly reduced their "long" exposure on the CME in early 2026 \(a tactical de-risking move\), the DAT Inflows throughout 2025 and 2026 remain at historically superior levels compared to the 2020-2024 period. This indicates that while short-term sentiment is cautious, the long-term structural demand for Bitcoin and Ethereum as institutional-grade assets remains firmly intact.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 697 0 R
/Prev 910 0 R
>>
endobj
